    "type_designations": ["ZK840"],
    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "The indicating device is designated the Avery Weigh-Tronix ZK840. The indicator is self-indicating, mains, DC or battery-powered, and is designed to be used as part of a Class III, Non-automatic Weighing Instrument. The load receptor(s) may be BSQ digital bases and/or conventional platforms fitted with load cells. Construction: plastic (ABS) enclosure, mountable to a BSQ base or alternatively desk/wall mounted using an optional bracket; ISTN LCD display capable of positive and negative images; 6 operational keys plus touchscreen soft keys. Devices include: single or multi-range (maximum of 3 partial ranges), semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, pre-set tare, recall of gross indication when tare is active, determination and indication of stability of equilibrium, checking of display, printing, gravity compensation, real time clock, command via external device (PC), counting, accumulation, checkweighing, target weighing, percentage weighing, grading, pick lists, kitting, density formulation, % recipe, gross/net/tare/preset tare/print/zero/motion/over-under weight/%PCWT/battery indicators, connection to additional load receptors with identification of active load receptor(s), PLUs, piece weight selection, extended indicating. Interfaces: BSQ digital base interface, 3 x logic level inputs, 3 x open collector outputs, 2 x RS232 serial ports, 10/100 Ethernet, USB Device, USB Host. Sealing: calibration and legally relevant parameters protected via physical (sealed jumper on main board) or software means (password and incrementing counters); access to electronics, jumper and load cell connections prevented via tamper-evident seals or wire seals."
  },
